WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.049 --> 00:00:05.150
The One Piece manga finally answered one of
THE BIGGEST AND MOST IMPORTANT questions of

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:11.420
this recent flashback by showing us that Jewelry
Bonney is indeed the daughter of the Revolutionary

00:00:11.420 --> 00:00:12.420
Ginny.

00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:17.050
But while we finally had that relationship
confirmed now we have WAY MORE questions than

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:18.270
we started with.

00:00:18.270 --> 00:00:22.930
Because in this chapter we were told that
Ginny was apparently kidnapped and forced

00:00:22.930 --> 00:00:25.260
to become the wife of a world noble.

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:27.720
So maybe she was sold by slavers or something.

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:34.260
But wow, out of all the options we discussed
for Bonney’s father like Kuma or Dragon,

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:39.450
Oda chose THE DARKEST WAY that this backstory
could go.

00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:44.340
I mean yeah, we’ve always known that Celestial
Dragons can just randomly pick people and

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:48.790
force them to become their wives, like we
saw in chapter 499.

00:00:48.790 --> 00:00:55.970
But man, seeing it like this and that Bonney
is the child of this forced marriage is a

00:00:55.970 --> 00:00:59.540
whole different level of messed up.

00:00:59.540 --> 00:01:06.560
Oda is seriously ramping up the tragic meter
to a whole other level.

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:11.299
But to make things even worse for Ginny, we
next see her two years later and she has somehow

00:01:11.299 --> 00:01:14.280
been struck by a deadly disease.

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:19.229
Unfortunately, instead of getting help she
is kicked out of Mary Geoise and left alone

00:01:19.229 --> 00:01:20.229
to die.

00:01:20.229 --> 00:01:27.070
Which is where we see her next in one of THE
MOST heartbreaking moments in recent one piece.

00:01:27.070 --> 00:01:32.870
Because with her dying breaths Ginny calls
Kuma and tells him once again that she loves

00:01:32.870 --> 00:01:33.870
him.

00:01:33.870 --> 00:01:37.310
And man, I won’t lie and say that I didn’t
tear up a bit when I saw that.

00:01:37.310 --> 00:01:43.080
I don’t think Oda has ever done a better
job of making me so emotionally invested in

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:45.189
two characters in a flashback.

00:01:45.189 --> 00:01:50.600
I mean Ginny and Kuma’s story is up there
with Law and Corazon for me.

00:01:50.600 --> 00:01:56.409
They’ve been through slavery, poverty, pain,
hunger, and years spent together as kids and

00:01:56.409 --> 00:01:57.710
later as revolutionaries.

00:01:57.710 --> 00:02:02.799
Which makes it even more tragic when Kuma
is eventually able to identify where Ginny

00:02:02.799 --> 00:02:09.080
is and he instantly pushes himself there using
his devil fruit, but what he finds is honestly

00:02:09.080 --> 00:02:11.270
just so tragic.

00:02:11.270 --> 00:02:15.460
Ginny is dead, with a baby Bonney in her arms.

00:02:15.460 --> 00:02:16.460
I mean, whew…

00:02:16.460 --> 00:02:17.550
I don’t know guys…

00:02:17.550 --> 00:02:21.510
This one hit me HARD.

00:02:21.510 --> 00:02:27.849
Oda has built up Kuma as this impossibly kind
and compassionate figure and now he’s had

00:02:27.849 --> 00:02:32.510
one of the only people who he truly cared
for ripped away.

00:02:32.510 --> 00:02:40.069
It’s truly heartbreaking, and just continues
to make me hate the celestial dragons more

00:02:40.069 --> 00:02:42.460
and more.

00:02:42.460 --> 00:02:49.550
What’s interesting though is that this scene
seems to confirm Bonney’s age to be around

00:02:49.550 --> 00:02:52.970
twelve years old since this happened about
twelve years ago.

00:02:52.970 --> 00:02:57.709
Which has crazy implications for the present
story, but before we move on from Ginny I

00:02:57.709 --> 00:03:01.350
want to quickly speculate on who this might
this evil person that Ginny was forced to

00:03:01.350 --> 00:03:02.459
marry might be.

00:03:02.459 --> 00:03:09.890
And I have one crazy theory that is just incredibly
twisted.

00:03:09.890 --> 00:03:10.890
Listen to this.

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:16.030
We don’t get much evidence on who Bonney’s
father is from the chapter, but let’s go

00:03:16.030 --> 00:03:17.989
back again to chapter 499.

00:03:17.989 --> 00:03:27.180
This is the first chapter we ever meet this
world noble, Saint Charlos, and this entire

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:32.640
scene might actually be some INSANE foreshadowing.

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:37.860
Because as soon as Charlos is introduced,
he kicks an injured man and then decides to

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:41.030
take this random nurse as his wife.

00:03:41.030 --> 00:03:46.580
This woman, by the way, was already engaged
to be married, which is kinda similar to the

00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:48.230
Ginny and Kuma situation.

00:03:48.230 --> 00:03:51.830
But what’s most interesting is what happens
next.

00:03:51.830 --> 00:03:59.300
Because then Zoro shows up and nearly causes
massive chaos by cutting down Charlos.

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:04.430
Fortunately for Zoro though Bonney steps in
and uses her powers to get him out of trouble.

00:04:04.430 --> 00:04:11.579
And now I’m just sitting here wondering
if Oda intentionally showed us Bonney’s

00:04:11.579 --> 00:04:18.150
powers FOR THE VERY FIRST TIME in the EXACT
SAME CHAPTER where a world noble kidnapped

00:04:18.150 --> 00:04:20.070
a woman to make them their wife.

00:04:20.070 --> 00:04:25.370
I mean, wow, seriously how insane is it that
and almost exactly six hundred chapters later,

00:04:25.370 --> 00:04:29.759
we are shown the very same thing happened
to Bonney’s own mother.

00:04:29.759 --> 00:04:35.910
So as much as it hurts me to say this, this
may have been some twisted foreshadowing about

00:04:35.910 --> 00:04:37.650
Bonney’s actual father.

00:04:37.650 --> 00:04:43.310
Because if we take this scene in chapter 499
as foreshadowing then wouldn’t it make sense

00:04:43.310 --> 00:04:48.750
that Bonney’s mother was married to Charlos’
father, who is Saint Roswald, whom we met

00:04:48.750 --> 00:04:51.720
just a few chapters before this scene?

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:58.340
And to make even more connections, in chapter
497 Roswald killed a slave who also had his

00:04:58.340 --> 00:05:02.300
own wife and child, which yeah is kinda a
loose connection to Ginny and Bonney, but

00:05:02.300 --> 00:05:07.130
I’m just saying that having all this all
occur so close together could have been hinting

00:05:07.130 --> 00:05:09.270
at Bonney’s father all along.

00:05:09.270 --> 00:05:16.380
But if you want a more concrete bit of evidence
just look at chapter 908, when we see Bonney

00:05:16.380 --> 00:05:18.350
sneaking into Mary Geoise.

00:05:18.350 --> 00:05:24.280
In this same scene, Kuma is shown being ridden
by who else, but Saint Roswald.

00:05:24.280 --> 00:05:29.180
Which could all just be some sort of horribly
tragic joke that Ginny was forced to marry

00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:32.160
the man who later rode Kuma around like a
horse.

00:05:32.160 --> 00:05:37.550
Man, if this is all true, then Oda has gone
to a whole other level of twisted in this

00:05:37.550 --> 00:05:41.830
backstory.

00:05:41.830 --> 00:05:48.539
And if Roswald is Bonney’s father, then
that actually means Bonney is related to Charlos

00:05:48.539 --> 00:05:51.090
and his sister.

00:05:51.090 --> 00:05:52.630
Which is just, uhh.

00:05:52.630 --> 00:05:53.630
Terrible.

00:05:53.630 --> 00:05:54.630
Awful.

00:05:54.630 --> 00:05:56.080
I don’t want that thought in my brain.

00:05:56.080 --> 00:06:01.170
However, it is entirely possible that Ginny
was married to some other random World Noble

00:06:01.170 --> 00:06:02.650
that we’ve never heard of.

00:06:02.650 --> 00:06:08.590
Or if we want to name other important nobles
perhaps someone like Garling, which would

00:06:08.590 --> 00:06:15.919
somehow mean that Bonney and Shanks are related,
possibly either as siblings or cousins.

00:06:15.919 --> 00:06:21.130
Taking it one step further, what if it was
even one of the Gorosei.

00:06:21.130 --> 00:06:25.990
I mean we’ve never seen them with children
or wives or anything like that, but maybe

00:06:25.990 --> 00:06:30.900
that is why Bonney is just bursting with tears
when fighting Saturn at the end of chapter

00:06:30.900 --> 00:06:32.970
1094.

00:06:32.970 --> 00:06:38.570
Surely these tears we see in this panel have
to mean Bonney is feeling some sort of deeper

00:06:38.570 --> 00:06:41.900
feelings than just hatred for Saturn.

00:06:41.900 --> 00:06:46.319
Obviously, it is suggested that Saturn is
the one who ordered Kuma’s memories erased,

00:06:46.319 --> 00:06:51.880
but what if it is more than that and Saturn
is the one who forced Ginny to marry him?

00:06:51.880 --> 00:06:57.520
In fact, one theory from WorstGenHQ on twitter
suggests that maybe Saturn was the one who

00:06:57.520 --> 00:07:00.990
caused Ginny’s deadly disease in the first
place.

00:07:00.990 --> 00:07:05.810
Maybe somehow it was a side effect of Saturn’s
demon-like abilities that made Ginny and Bonney

00:07:05.810 --> 00:07:07.350
sick in the first place.

00:07:07.350 --> 00:07:13.090
And if that is true, then if Bonney is somehow
able to kill Saturn by the end of this arc

00:07:13.090 --> 00:07:15.780
it would certainly be fitting justice.

00:07:15.780 --> 00:07:23.050
And while this is all getting a bit too dark
for my tastes, if any of these options are

00:07:23.050 --> 00:07:28.020
true, and Oda’s not just hiding her real
father somehow, then that means that Bonney

00:07:28.020 --> 00:07:31.520
actually has Celestial Dragon blood in her
veins.

00:07:31.520 --> 00:07:36.430
Which just makes me incredibly curious why
they would throw her out with her mother without

00:07:36.430 --> 00:07:38.050
even trying to save her.

00:07:38.050 --> 00:07:42.841
I mean, Ginny wasn’t a Celestial Dragon,
so that makes sense that they wouldn’t care

00:07:42.841 --> 00:07:49.290
about her dying, but Bonney being at least
half-blood has to mean something, right?

00:07:49.290 --> 00:07:53.550
Could this play some role later on in the
conflict between Bonney and Saturn?

00:07:53.550 --> 00:07:59.430
Although, honestly it seems like the demon
Saturn is showing absolutely no hesitation

00:07:59.430 --> 00:08:04.710
in trying to kill Bonney, so either he doesn’t
care about her lineage or she doesn’t actually

00:08:04.710 --> 00:08:06.430
have noble blood in the first place.

00:08:06.430 --> 00:08:16.430
Or to throw just one more crazy idea out there,
what if Oda is still faking use out and Bonney

00:08:16.430 --> 00:08:18.990
still isn’t Ginny’s daughter?

00:08:18.990 --> 00:08:23.770
And sure, call me crazy, but we’ve been
wrong about assumptions like this in the past,

00:08:23.770 --> 00:08:26.470
so I’m not ruling it out just yet.

00:08:26.470 --> 00:08:32.080
In fact, I also still think the clone option
is still on the table and could explain how

00:08:32.080 --> 00:08:35.279
Bonney is alive, but more on that in just
a minute.

00:08:35.279 --> 00:08:39.210
And while her father’s identity remains
a mystery, I’m also highly interested in

00:08:39.210 --> 00:08:43.240
figuring out this strange disease that affected
Bonney and her mother.

00:08:43.240 --> 00:08:49.410
It is called Sapphire Scale, and it is even
rarer than the Amber Lead disease that wiped

00:08:49.410 --> 00:08:52.370
out Law’s entire town during his flashback.

00:08:52.370 --> 00:08:57.019
And what we know about this disease is that
when people who have the disease go out in

00:08:57.019 --> 00:09:02.740
the sun or moon light, their entire body starts
to turn blue and their skin becomes hard,

00:09:02.740 --> 00:09:05.079
like rock or some sort of tough animal scales.

00:09:05.079 --> 00:09:11.020
Now, we aren’t told how she got this disease
or if it is contagious, but if it is anything

00:09:11.020 --> 00:09:15.530
like the Amber Lead disease, then it might
be caused by something horrible that the world

00:09:15.530 --> 00:09:17.339
nobles were doing.

00:09:17.339 --> 00:09:23.589
If you remember from Law’s flashback, Law’s
hometown would mine this Amber Ore which was

00:09:23.589 --> 00:09:28.450
actually deathly poisonous over time and could
be passed down through generations.

00:09:28.450 --> 00:09:33.200
Which seems to also have happened in this
case since Bonney also has the disease.

00:09:33.200 --> 00:09:37.899
And I honestly have no idea what could have
caused it other than maybe some government

00:09:37.899 --> 00:09:46.740
experimentation or maybe a side-effect of
one of the Gorosei’s demon powers or something.

00:09:46.740 --> 00:09:56.260
But this leaves us with the question of how
did Bonney live while her mother died?

00:09:56.260 --> 00:10:04.370
And the answer to this question is going to
have a HUGE effect on the rest of Kuma and

00:10:04.370 --> 00:10:05.490
Bonney’s story.

00:10:05.490 --> 00:10:11.079
Because we see in this chapter that Kuma took
care of Bonney for quite a long time.

00:10:11.079 --> 00:10:15.250
To protect her from the disease he kept her
out of the sunlight for YEARS.

00:10:15.250 --> 00:10:17.630
Can you just imagine that?

00:10:17.630 --> 00:10:19.870
Literally not being able to go outside.

00:10:19.870 --> 00:10:27.769
I know Kuma would bring her books and everything,
and we even finally learned the heart-breaking

00:10:27.769 --> 00:10:32.270
origin of his famous last question: “If
you could travel anywhere, where would you

00:10:32.270 --> 00:10:33.270
like to go?”

00:10:33.270 --> 00:10:38.209
Now though we get some more of the most wholesome
panels in the entire story as we see a young

00:10:38.209 --> 00:10:41.410
Bonney growing up with Kuma.

00:10:41.410 --> 00:10:46.450
And man while reading this I just couldn’t
help but wish that Kuma had agreed to marry

00:10:46.450 --> 00:10:48.280
Ginny all those years ago.

00:10:48.280 --> 00:10:51.860
Then they could have actually lived together
as a happy family.

00:10:51.860 --> 00:10:54.440
But man, I guess it was never meant to be.

00:10:54.440 --> 00:11:01.440
And even though we see these two spending
the years together, we just always knew this

00:11:01.440 --> 00:11:05.300
was going to end in some sort of tragedy.

00:11:05.300 --> 00:11:10.200
But sadly they couldn’t live like this forever
because a doctor told Kuma that the disease

00:11:10.200 --> 00:11:13.690
would still kill her by the time she was ten
years old.

00:11:13.690 --> 00:11:16.370
So how was she cured?

00:11:16.370 --> 00:11:23.459
Well, one option is that Kuma used his Paw
devil fruit to somehow push the disease out

00:11:23.459 --> 00:11:24.510
of Bonney.

00:11:24.510 --> 00:11:31.770
Which sounds crazy, but we’ve been seeing
Kuma push out things like pain, so it isn’t

00:11:31.770 --> 00:11:35.380
unreasonable to think the Kuma could push
this disease.

00:11:35.380 --> 00:11:41.930
However, like we just saw in chapter 1097,
someone would have to take in that disease

00:11:41.930 --> 00:11:45.940
which means that Kuma might have absorbed
the disease himself to save Bonney.

00:11:45.940 --> 00:11:50.470
Now whether he was just strong enough to survive
the disease or it didn’t affect him because

00:11:50.470 --> 00:11:52.769
of his Buccaneer blood, we aren’t really
sure.

00:11:52.769 --> 00:11:58.690
But if you look at this small flashback in
chapter 1072, it does appear Kuma has some

00:11:58.690 --> 00:12:03.720
bandages on his entire body, so I wonder if
this could be some sort of side-effect from

00:12:03.720 --> 00:12:05.300
this Sapphire Scale disease.

00:12:05.300 --> 00:12:10.310
Of course, another option for how Bonney lived
is that Kuma made some sort of deal with the

00:12:10.310 --> 00:12:12.340
world nobles to save Bonney.

00:12:12.340 --> 00:12:16.870
And the easiest way for this to work would
be that Kuma basically sold himself to the

00:12:16.870 --> 00:12:22.519
world nobles in exchange for medicine or possibly
even Bonney’s age devil fruit.

00:12:22.519 --> 00:12:27.950
I mean, since the disease is indeed age-related
then Bonney’s fruit would be the perfect

00:12:27.950 --> 00:12:31.589
one to keep her from ever growing too old
too be killed.

00:12:31.589 --> 00:12:36.449
Although she definitely has aged herself up
past ten years old, which makes me wonder

00:12:36.449 --> 00:12:38.730
if that is true or not.

00:12:38.730 --> 00:12:44.880
Maybe that leaves open the option that the
real Bonney did die and the one we see now

00:12:44.880 --> 00:12:46.680
is a clone??

00:12:46.680 --> 00:12:50.490
I don’t know honestly, I’m still trying
to wrap my head around all of this

00:12:50.490 --> 00:12:57.829
But whatever the case, Bonney is alive, and
she is now confirmed to only be twelve years

00:12:57.829 --> 00:12:58.829
old.

00:12:58.829 --> 00:13:04.589
Which is just crazy to think that she’s
already gone around and become a famous pirate

00:13:04.589 --> 00:13:09.200
while still basically a child, but maybe her
devil fruit’s powers also affect her brain

00:13:09.200 --> 00:13:11.890
to match the age of her physical body.

00:13:11.890 --> 00:13:17.370
And it appears that in the next chapter we
are finally going to see Kuma earn his title

00:13:17.370 --> 00:13:20.070
of the Tyrant King of Sorbet kingdom.

00:13:20.070 --> 00:13:24.709
Because at the end of this one, the corrupt
king that the freedom fighter overthrew in

00:13:24.709 --> 00:13:29.149
chapter 1097 is back to cause trouble for
Sorbet Kingdom.

00:13:29.149 --> 00:13:34.050
And honestly I thought he had been killed
already, which I wish was true, because now

00:13:34.050 --> 00:13:39.240
I am predicting that someone is probably going
to try to take Bonney from Kuma, and man,

00:13:39.240 --> 00:13:42.180
that is not going to end well.

00:13:42.180 --> 00:13:49.399
I can just imagine Kuma destroying the ENTIRE
KINGDOM to try to save Bonney from being captured.

00:13:49.399 --> 00:13:54.050
On the other hand, maybe the corrupt king
takes everyone on the island hostage and Kuma

00:13:54.050 --> 00:13:56.839
is forced to trade himself to set them free.

00:13:56.839 --> 00:14:03.500
It would make sense because Kuma has consistently
sacrificed himself to protect these people

00:14:03.500 --> 00:14:08.579
over the years, so maybe he will take the
one option that sacrifices himself and saves

00:14:08.579 --> 00:14:10.209
everyone else.

00:14:10.209 --> 00:14:15.899
Or one more option to consider is that BOTH
Bonney and Kuma get taken in by the world

00:14:15.899 --> 00:14:16.899
government.

00:14:16.899 --> 00:14:20.740
Perhaps Kuma turns himself in to save the
people of Sorbet kingdom and then Bonney comes

00:14:20.740 --> 00:14:21.890
along as well.

00:14:21.890 --> 00:14:28.959
And this actually makes more sense than you
might think because we still have this unexplained

00:14:28.959 --> 00:14:34.279
panel of former admiral Akainu saying he was
worried when he learned that she escaped.

00:14:34.279 --> 00:14:39.460
And it doesn’t seem likely to me that he
was referring to when she was a literal baby,

00:14:39.460 --> 00:14:45.400
so there has to be some other time that she
was captured and then escaped from the world

00:14:45.400 --> 00:14:46.400
nobles.

00:14:46.400 --> 00:14:51.200
On top of that, if you look at Bonney and
Kizaru’s conversation from chapter 1092

00:14:51.200 --> 00:14:56.860
it does seem like Kizaru and Bonney have known
each other for quite some time as well.

00:14:56.860 --> 00:15:01.670
Kizaru even remarks that she’s grown quite
a bit taller, which makes me think he saw

00:15:01.670 --> 00:15:04.079
her some time when she was a kid.

00:15:04.079 --> 00:15:08.430
So with all of this, I’m really thinking
that Bonney was with Kuma for at least the

00:15:08.430 --> 00:15:15.389
start of when Kuma agreed to become a government
experiment and then she later escaped.

00:15:15.389 --> 00:15:22.380
However, one thing that is certain is that
Bonney and Kuma’s backstory is going right

00:15:22.380 --> 00:15:25.970
up there with the saddest in the entire story.

00:15:25.970 --> 00:15:31.459
And if you know one thing about sad backstories,
it is that every single straw hat has one.

00:15:31.459 --> 00:15:38.800
So there has never been a greater chance than
now for Bonney to join the crew.

00:15:38.800 --> 00:15:42.870
But if you don’t want to wait to see exactly
how Bonney would work on a crew with Luffy,

00:15:42.870 --> 00:15:49.350
I figured out how the entire Worst Generation
would get along on one crew, and you can check

00:15:49.350 --> 00:15:50.990
out that video right here.

00:15:50.990 --> 00:15:55.790
And I think we all probably saw the message
that Oda wasn’t able to finish the drawings

00:15:55.790 --> 00:15:56.790
for this chapter.

00:15:56.790 --> 00:15:59.769
So let’s all spare a prayer or some positive
thoughts that he is doing okay.

00:15:59.769 --> 00:16:04.230
He works super hard every week to bring us
this story that we love, and nothing could

00:16:04.230 --> 00:16:07.420
be worse than him overworking himself and
ruining his health.

00:16:07.420 --> 00:16:13.569
Personally, I think it might be time to shift
to One Piece being every other week so he

00:16:13.569 --> 00:16:14.740
has more time to rest.

00:16:14.740 --> 00:16:18.370
But anyways, Shanks for watching and I’ll
see you in the next one.

